# IANA backzone (almanac-sourced), Lesotho (Maseru) -- Maseru Mean Time (+1:50) until Mar
# 1903, then SAST (+2:00), with a SINGLE wartime summer at +3:00 (19 Sep 1943..19 Mar 1944);
# vs default link to Africa/Johannesburg, which ran the SA war-DST rule for TWO summers
# (1942-43 and 1943-44). Lesotho did NOT observe the first war summer, so it stands 1 hour
# BEHIND the default across 1942-09-20..1943-03-21; it also led the +1:30 default by ~20 min
# before Mar 1903.
#
# NOT Shanks-page-sourced: reproduces IANA's own backzone Africa/Maseru exactly (the Sierra
# Leone / Bahrain discipline). Window [1892-02-08, 1943-03-21); from the second war summer
# on, Maseru matches Johannesburg.
# Rebuild the compiled TZif with:  rake shanks:build.  Cross-check: IANA:Africa/Maseru.
Zone Shanks/LS_1 1:50:00  -    LMT   1903 Mar
                 2:00     -    SAST  1943 Sep 19  2:00
                 2:00     1:00 SAST  1944 Mar 19  2:00
                 2:00     -    SAST
